{
  "slug": "blueprint-sdlc",
  "name": "Blueprint Sdlc",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Blueprint SDLC — 27 slash commands that turn Claude Code into a disciplined engineering team. Full pipeline from /backlog through   /finish with 15-rule audit hooks, parallel subagent execution, and session crash recovery.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **27 skills**, **2 hooks** and **2 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (27): `address-pr` (Fetch PR review comments, categorize feedback, implement fixes, and push), `backlog` (Capture, manage, and promote pre-planning ideas before they become full plans), `batch-flow` (Execute multiple plans sequentially in a single session — loops flow-auto for plans N through M with auto…), `bp-branch` (Create a new feature branch following type/kebab-case conventions), `bp-commit` (Commit current changes following emoji+type conventions with code formatting), `bp-context` (Scan project and generate/audit CLAUDE.md files with stack auto-detection and Context7 docs), `bp-push` (Push the current branch to remote with branch safety checks), `bp-ship` (Commit and push changes in one go with branch safety checks), and 19 more\n- **Hooks** (2): `PreToolUse`, `Stop`\n- **MCP servers** (2): `context7`, `sequential-thinking`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install blueprint-sdlc@claude-community` from `skaisser/blueprint-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
